<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Robert Venables</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1613–1687</span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Robert Venables was an English soldier who commanded the land forces of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/oliver-cromwell">Oliver Cromwell</a>'s Western Design, with Admiral <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/william-penn">William Penn</a> leading the fleet. After their attack on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/santo-domingo">Santo Domingo</a> failed in April 1655, they captured <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jamaica">Jamaica</a> from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a> in May 1655. On their return to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/england">England</a> both commanders were briefly imprisoned in the Tower of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/london">London</a> for leaving their posts.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/robert-venables.jpg" alt="Robert Venables" width="320" height="256" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: by J. Ogilby · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Jamaica1671ogilby.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
